From 0bea968bef4389749ee2609c2b9cdddbcf60ad48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:45:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] codegen_c: pass data-less enums as their tag at C ABI
 boundaries

pngquant 3.0.3 crashed at runtime on ppc32 Darwin in pthread_mutex_lock
with a junk mutex pointer, under a `set_current_info` frame that had
been entered at +24 (past its own PIC-base setup). The C function it
calls, `pngquant_main_internal(options, liq) -> pngquant_error` (a C
`enum`), was declared in the generated C as returning
`struct e_..pngquant_error { uint32_t TAG; }`. Darwin ppc32 returns every
struct through a hidden pointer in r3, so Rust called (out, &options, liq)
while C read (options, liq) = (junk, &options); the junk `log_callback`
field later got called. The same mismatch hit every C call into the
Rust-defined `liq_set_*` (returning `liq_error`).

0043's scalar wrappers (`get_cabi_scalar`: imports, Rust definitions and
C ABI function pointers) only knew newtypes and non-zero-niche enums.
A data-less enum (`Values`/`Linear` variants, only unit variants) is now
passed and returned as its tag too, as C declares it (`enum`/`int`, or
`uint8_t` for `#[repr(u8)]`). Tag-plus-data enums still fail the
single-field check and stay aggregates.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/trans/codegen_c.cpp | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/trans/codegen_c.cpp b/src/trans/codegen_c.cpp
index be76db1b..f09eff35 100644
--- a/src/trans/codegen_c.cpp
+++ b/src/trans/codegen_c.cpp
@@ -1798,8 +1798,9 @@ namespace {
             }
             return ty.data().is_Function();
         }
-        /// If `ty` is emitted as a C struct but is passed as a single scalar (a newtype, or an enum using a non-zero niche
-        /// such as `Option<&T>`), return that scalar's type.
+        /// If `ty` is emitted as a C struct but is passed as a single scalar (a newtype, an enum using a non-zero niche
+        /// such as `Option<&T>`, or a data-less enum such as a `#[repr(C)]` error code, which is its tag), return that
+        /// scalar's type.
         const ::HIR::TypeRef* get_cabi_scalar(const ::HIR::TypeRef& ty) const
         {
             const ::HIR::TypeRef* cur = &ty;
@@ -1833,7 +1834,10 @@ namespace {
                 if( !repr ) {
                     return nullptr;
                 }
-                if( is_enum && !repr->variants.is_NonZero() ) {
+                // Enums: a non-zero niche (`Option<&T>`), or a tag with no (non-ZST) data (`Values`/`Linear` with
+                // unit variants: the C side declares `enum`/`int`/`uint8_t`). A tag plus data is a real aggregate on
+                // both sides and fails the single-field check below.
+                if( is_enum && !(repr->variants.is_NonZero() || repr->variants.is_Values() || repr->variants.is_Linear()) ) {
                     return nullptr;
                 }
                 // Must be exactly one non-zero-sized field, covering the whole type
